# <type>: <imperative summary, <= 72 chars>
#
# Types: feat | fix | refactor | perf | test | docs | build | ci | chore | release
#
# Why, not what -- the diff already shows what. Explain the reasoning a reader cannot recover from
# the code, and name the evidence:
#
#   Evidence: gate PASS (build clean; typecheck 0 errors; freshness ok).
#
# One blank line between the summary and the body.
#
# This repository credits exactly one author, Dhira Wigata <dwigata.putra@gmail.com>.
#
#   - No Co-authored-by, Co-developed-by, Generated-by or Assisted-by trailer.
#   - No "Generated with ..." byline or footer, and no robot emoji credit line.
#   - Agents assist; they do not author. Work an agent did is described in the body as prose, which
#     is honest and needs no trailer.
#   - Signed-off-by is allowed: it is Dhira's own `git commit -s` sign-off, not a second author.
#
# The rule applies to the subject and the body alike, and CI checks the whole history -- not just
# this commit -- for a single identity and for authorship trailers.
#
# Set the identity repo-locally before the first commit, never globally:
#   git config --local user.name  "Dhira Wigata"
#   git config --local user.email "dwigata.putra@gmail.com"
